Lyreo.wikitext:
{{UltramarinesPortal}}
'''Lyreo''' was an [[Intercessor]] in the [[Ultramarines]]' [[Combat Squad Damocles]], which was part of the [[Chapter]]'s [[2nd Company (Ultramarines)|2nd Company]].{{Fn|1a}}
==History==
{{Spoiler|source=Space Marine II}}
The [[Combat Squad Damocles|Squad]] was originally under the command of [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] [[Gadriel]], when the [[2nd Company (Ultramarines)|2nd Company]] aided in the defense of the [[Tyranid]] invaded [[Recidious System]]. However after [[Demetrian Titus]] was reinstated into the [[Ultramarines]] as a [[Space Marine Lieutenant|Lieutenant]], the [[Company]]'s [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]], [[Sevastus Acheran]], gave Titus command of Damocles. He then charged the Squad with re-securing the [[Orbital Defence Cannon]]s on [[Kadaku]], which had been swarmed by Tyranids, so that the [[Imperial]] forces in the [[System]] could finish the evacuation of the doomed world. The [[Cadian 8th]] had been tasked with protecting the Cannons, until the Tyranids began overwhelming them and the [[Regiment]] was forced to retreat. When the [[Thunderhawk]] [[Absolver (Thunderhawk)|Absolver]], deployed the Squad at the Cadians' new location, they met with [[Major]] [[Sarkaana]] who informed them of the situation.{{Fn|1a}} 

Upon learning that the [[Tyranids]] were continuing to launch assaults against the [[Regiment]], [[Demetrian Titus|Titus]] charged Lyreo with helping the [[Cadian 8th]] secure their location, with the aid of the [[Combat Squad Damocles|Squad]] members [[Altareus]] and [[Elion]]. The [[Space Marine Lieutenant|Lieutenant]], meanwhile would take [[Gadriel]] and [[Chairon]] to reclaim the [[Orbital Defence Cannon]]s. Once the area was secure, though, the three were to rejoin Titus and aid in reclaiming the Cannons as well. However before they could do so, [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Sevastus Acheran]] gave Lyreo, Altareus and Elion new orders to carry out on [[Kadaku]]. The [[Intercessor]] informed Titus of this and stated the Lieutenant's group would have to reclaim the Cannons on their own.{{Fn|1a}} As they carried out their Captain's orders, though, the three were swarmed by [[Hormagaunt]]s and Elion became separated from the others. After Lyreo and Altareus defeated the Tyranids, they discovered that he had been killed during the battle. Some type of Tyranid had put a hole clean through Elion's head, which a sorrowful Lyreo shared with Titus of after both of their missions had been completed.{{Fn|1b}}

Shortly after this, [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Sevastus Acheran]] ordered [[Combat Squad Damocles]] to return to [[Kadaku]] and evacuate an important asset to the [[Battle Barge]] [[Resilient]]. This turned out to be the [[Archmagos]] [[Nozick Beta-12]], who had been working on a [[Project Aurora|secret project]] and refused to leave until he collected data from his invaded facility. Thanks to the efforts of the [[8th Cadian]] and other [[Ultramarines]], the Archmagos had been taken from there before the Tyranids could harm him and then secured within an [[Astra Militarum]] base, where the [[Thunderhawk]] [[Absolver (Thunderhawk)|Absolver]] touched down at. After talking to Nozick, Titus learned that the Archmagos' data would have to be manually transmitted to him, by someone within the facility. The [[Space Marine Lieutenant|Lieutenant]] took on the task with the aid of [[Gadriel]] and [[Chairon]], while leaving Lyreo and [[Altareus]] to guard the Archmagos. The Astra Militarum base was later under attack by the [[Tyranids]], when Nozick successfully received the data from Titus. Though they were still near the facility, the Lieutenant told Lyreo to immediately board the Absolver and evacuate the Archmagos to the Resilient. The order was obeyed at once, and the two [[Intercessors]] left with Nozick aboard the Thunderhawk, along with the Archmagos' research.{{Fn|1b}} 

However before they could get far, the [[Thunderhawk]] was wracked with explosions and began to crash. No one on the ground has seen what had hit the [[Absolver (Thunderhawk)|Absolver]], but it had landed in an area held by the [[Tyranids]]. When [[Demetrian Titus|Titus]], [[Gadriel]] and [[Chairon]] reached the Thunderhawk,{{Fn|1b}} they could see that everyone aboard it had died.{{Fn|1c}} This had been no accident, though, as the Absolver's remains were daubed with the markings of [[Chaos]], along with the name of [[Imurah]] and that [[Nozick Beta-12|Nozick]] had been purposely impaled upon a part the Thunderhawk's wreckage.{{Fn|1b}} It was soon discovered, that this had been the work of the [[Thousand Sons]] [[Sorcerer Lord]] [[Imurah]], who then launched his own invasion of the [[Recidious System]].{{Fn|1d}} 
