Lyrmund Thall.wikitext:
{{ImperialFistsPortal}}
'''Lyrmund Thall''' was a [[Castellan (Imperial Fists)|Castellan]] in the [[Imperial Fists]] [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]], who took part in the [[Horus Heresy]].{{Fn|1}}

==Biography==
He was among the [[Imperial Fists]] that defended [[Beta-Garmon II]], when [[Warmaster]] [[Horus Lupercal]]'s [[Traitor]] forces [[Battle of Beta-Garmon|invaded]] the [[Beta-Garmon Star Cluster]].{{Fn|1}}

By 009.[[M31]] the [[Imperium]]'s forces were mired in brutal attritional warfare on the world, when a counter-thrust led by the [[Emperor's Children]] and [[Alpha Legion]] threatened to let the Traitors [[Battle of Nyrcon|seize]] the vital fortress-city [[Nyrcon]]. However, as Thall led its defence, the [[Disciples of the Flames]] suddenly appeared and began attacking the flank of the Traitors' forces. This sent the invaders in disarray and the [[Castellan (Imperial Fists)|Castellan]] took advantage of this by leading his own forces against the Traitors as well and sending a cohort of his Mechanicum allies to aid the Disciples. Their commander, [[Cassian Dracos]], would not respond to Thall's attempts to make contact with him and soon led the Disciples farther away from Nyrcon. They had come to follow one of Dracos' prophecies and would not stop their advance to aid in defending the fortress-city. Soon the Castellan had no choice but to stop his own advance and began defending the territory the Disciples had aided in recovering. However, not all of Thall's forces heeded his orders. For reasons unknown, the Mechanicum cohort refused to return and clung close to Dracos, while a number of [[Salamanders]] the Castellan had commanded also left to join the Disciples. With no word of their [[Primarch]] [[Vulkan]], they chose to follow Dracos, as he was once the Salamanders' [[Legion Master]].{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [https://www.warhammer-community.com/2022/11/22/horus-heresy-exemplary-battles-scorch-the-heads-of-the-hydra-with-faith-and-flame/ Warhammer Community: Horus Heresy Exemplary Battles – Scorch the Heads of the Hydra With Faith and Flame (Posted on 22/11/2022)] - [https://www.warhammer-community.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/tY1xCtj3G3KDp1KS.pdf The Battle of Nyrcon City: Visions in the Flames PDF], pgs. 2-4 ''(last accessed 22 November 2022)''

