Lyros Sydance.wikitext:
{{UltramarinesPortal}}
'''Lyros Sydance''' was a [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] of the [[Ultramarines]] [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]] at the onset of the [[Horus Heresy]].{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|1b}}

==History==
During the [[Great Crusade]] (roughly eight years before the [[Battle of Calth]]), Sydance led the main assault on the [[Eldar]] [[Craftworld]] [[Jielthwa]]. During the charge, he was cut off and ended up fighting and killing a dozen Eldar warriors single-handedly before being reinforced by [[Remus Ventanus]]. Although Sydance was decorated by [[Roboute Guilliman|his]] [[Primarch]] for this achievement, Sydance and Ventanus noted that there were actually thirteen bodies in the hall where the fight took place, remarking that there was a high probability that the last kill was made by Ventanus (who had come in firing). Thus, it became a standing joke between the two that Sydance was decorated for twelve kills whereas Ventanus had only made one, but that Ventanus's may have been crucial.{{Fn|1b}}

During the [[Battle of Calth]], Sydance was commanding the [[4th Company (Ultramarines Legion)|4th Company]]. Sydance survived the initial [[Word Bearers]] assault and fought under Captain Ventanus when he took command of their mustered forces.{{Fn|1b}}

