'''M'Shen''' was the [[Callidus Temple|Callidus assassin]] who killed the rebel [[Primarch]] [[Konrad Curze|Night Haunter]].

==Biography==
During the early [[Horus Heresy]], when the [[Officio Assassinorum]] was still attempting to kill [[Horus]] through their standard method of sending lone operatives, [[Siress Callidus]] suggested sending M'Shen to kill Horus after the failure of the [[Venenum Assassin]] [[Tobeld]], referring to her as ''"...one of the best of my clade..."''. Ultimately, however, the [[Master of Assassins]] decided to instead assemble the first ever [[Execution Force]] (a team made up of assassins from multiple clades).{{Fn|3a}} M'Shen was not chosen as the Callidus' representative (that role instead being assigned to [[Koyne]]).{{Fn|3b}}

Later, M'Shen was assigned to assassinate the Traitor Primarch Konrad Curze. Evidentially he already knew he was the target of an assassin, and only allowed himself to be killed to "vindicate" his rebellion against the Imperium, and show that he was right to destroy [[Nostramo]]. She took many of his precious items as personal trinkets, and cut off his head to take to her masters. She later declared to the [[Talos Valcoran|Soul Hunter]] she would be remembered as Godslayer. On her way back to her ship, she briefly fought Soul Hunter, but made it back to her ship.{{Fn|1}}

Ultimately M'Shen was brutally killed and mutilated by the Soul Hunter as he pursued her from [[Tsagualsa]]. Her death was foreseen by the Night Haunter, who although he ordered his legion to allow her to escape, knew that first the Soul Hunter, and then the rest of the legion would disobey his final order.{{Fn|1}} However, the vid-log built into M´Shen's vambraces somehow managed to reach Terra, showing the screaming gallery and containing the alleged final words of [[Night Haunter]].{{Fn|2}}

==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
*M'shen is likely a reference to the real-life actor [[Wikipedia:Martin Sheen|Martin Sheen]], whose character, Captain Benjamin Willard, is sent to assassinate rebel Colonel Walter E. Kurtz in the film ''[[Wikipedia:Apocalypse Now|Apocalypse Now]]'' (who himself is an inspiration for the Primarch Konrad Curze).

