Maelon Dhrost.wikitext:
{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
'''Maelon Dhrost''' is a [[Cadian]] [[General]] of the [[Astra Militarum]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
[[Image:Dhorst.jpg|thumb|right|[[General]] Maelon Dhrost and his standard{{Fn|1}}]]
Dhrost is something of a hero to his men, though in truth he has served the [[Astra Militarum|Militarum]] for so long, that the [[General]] has little compassion left for the common soldiery. Men come and go, but war is eternal. Being a stalwart foe of the [[Ruinous Powers]], Dhrost knows full well that victory against the horrors of the universe will always come at a high price. Amongst all of those who wore the binary star icon of the [[Cryptus Campaign]], Dhrost alone realized the cost the system’s defenders would have to pay.{{Fn|1}}

As the [[Cryptus Campaign|Campaign]] began in in 998.[[M41]], he commanded the [[Astra Militarum]]'s forces that defended [[Asphodex]], but the [[Tyranids]] of [[Hive Fleet Leviathan]] overwhelmed them. As the world began to fall to the [[Xenos]], the [[Blood Angels]] and [[Flesh Tearers]] arrived to save the [[Cryptus System]], due to its closeness to the [[Baal System]]. Led by the Blood Angels [[Chapter Master|Commander]], [[Dante]], the [[Space Marines]] dispersed and fought the Tyranids. Dante himself led his Chapter's forces on [[Asphodex]], where the found [[General]] Dhrost and the remnants of the Astra Militarum Regiments he commanded. They would fight together to try and save the world, but like before the Tyranids proved to be too powerful. This led Dante to make an alliance with the [[Necrons]] of the [[Mephrit Dynasty]], who dwelt within the Cryptus System. This alliance saw the activation of a [[Magnovitrium|powerful weapon]] the Dynasty possessed, which inflicted heavy casualties amongst the Tyranids. However it was not enough to stop Hive Fleet Leviathan and Dante declared the System was lost to the ravenous Xenos. He then ordered for any surviving civilian or military forces to be evacuated, as the Blood Angels' fleet prepared to retreat back to the Chapter's [[Adeptus Astartes Homeworld|Homeworld]] of [[Baal]]. As the Tyranids attacked their position on Asphodex, Dante ordered for Dhrost and his surviving forces to prepare to be evacuated. Dhrost was amongst the last of the Astra Militarum to leave and the General spared one last look at the world he had tried to save{{Fn|2a}}:
{{QuoteBox
|quote = '''''I did what I could. I leave three million dead men here. I pray it was enough.'''''{{Fn|2a}}
|align = center
|width = 26em
}}   
[[Dante]] and the [[Blood Angels]] evacuated soon afterwards{{Fn|2a}} and the [[Imperium]]'s surviving spaceships in the [[Cryptus System]] gathered together, as they prepared to leave the [[System]]. As these preparations were underway, Dante called for his [[Chapter]] to have a [[Red Council]] meeting, to discuss how to defend [[Baal]] against the advancing [[Hive Fleet Leviathan]], as the Imperials' fleet made their way to the Blood Angels' [[Adeptus Astartes Homeworld|Homeworld]]. [[General]] Dhrost and his fellow high ranking survivor [[Sister Superior]] [[Amity Hope]] were allowed to attend the meeting by Dante, despite not being of the Chapter. Soon the matter of what to do with the Cryptus System's two million surviving citizens came up and Dante remarked that many would soon die, as there were not enough supplies to feed them all. The [[Chapter Master|Commander]] declared that the survivors would need to be settled in other [[System]]s as a result of this and [[General]] Dhrost said that he would take the survivors to [[Cadia]], where the [[Fortress World]] would take in as many as possible. When [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Karlaen]] remarked on how Cadia lay near the [[Eye of Terror]], Dhrost declared that despite that, the Fortress World was still vastly safer than other Imperial worlds.{{Fn|2b}} 

[[Dante]] stated the [[Blood Angels]] would do their part as well and settle as many survivors as possible in the [[Baal System]], while also taking [[Aspirants]] from the population to restrengthen their [[Chapter]]. Due to how far [[Cadia]] was from the [[Cryptus System]], however, the [[Chapter Master|Commander]] declared that the survivors would need to be settled on Imperial worlds closer to the System as well. In order to best solve this problem, Dante decided to provide the [[General]] with a letter of demand from the Blood Angels, requesting assistance in the matter. Dante then told Dhrost, that as the General was leading the survivors to Cadia, he was to present the letter to the [[Imperial Commander]]s of the worlds that laid beyond the [[Red Scar]]. As [[Hive Fleet Leviathan]] continued its advance, many of these worlds would request the Chapter's protection and Dante remarked that if their Commanders' wished for the Blood Angels' aid, then they would need to take in as many of Cryptus' survivors as possible.{{Fn|2b}}

Though [[Cadia]] was later [[Dead World|destroyed]], during the [[13th Black Crusade]],{{Fn|3}} Dhrost survived its death and continues to serve the [[Imperium]].{{Fn|4}}

