==Appearance and Abilities==
A slender and unassuming figure dressed in pale robes, at first glance Malcador appeared no different from a thousand other [[Administratum]] functionaries, except for his staff of office and the force of his psychic presence.{{Fn|3b}} Malcador appeared to be very frail and sickly, and in fact this was an image he deliberately cultivated in order to have his enemies underestimate his formidable power. However as the Heresy wore on, Malcador's haggard appearance became more and more the reality.{{Fn|14}}

Malcador wore an [[archaeotech]] collar around his neck, which was capable of generating a powerful force field that would redirect an enemy's attack back at them. His staff was capable of unleashing a wave of nuclear fire, but Malcador states that this was a tool rather than a weapon.{{Fn|19}}

Malcador was the most powerful human psyker in the [[galaxy]] after the Emperor himself and potentially [[Magnus the Red]],{{Fn|5a}} and demonstrated this psychic ability on several occasions. During the aforementioned confrontation at [[Monarchia]], he showed physical resilience unnatural for a man of his apparent age and frailty; when smashed from his feet by the [[primarch]] [[Lorgar]], he landed on broken ground after a distance of some twenty metres, and survived with but a few broken bones. He also demonstrated telekinetic ability, retrieving his fallen staff and bringing it sharply into his hand.{{Fn|4a}}

Sometime during the [[Great Crusade]], Malcador easily incapacitated [[Horus]] with his psychic abilities after the [[Primarch]] attempted to utter the name of one of the [[Lost Primarch]]s. Malcador reverted into a deep, dark rage complete with a rictus grin that was described as an older familiar rage.{{Fn|18}}

