Malya L'nor.wikitext:
{{ImperiumPortal}}
'''Malya L'nor''' was one of the leaders of the pro-[[Imperium]] resistance on [[Quintus]], which opposed the rule of the [[Daemon Prince]] [[Kernax Voldorius|Voldorius]] when he subjugated the planet.{{Fn|1a}}

==Biography==
Prior to the invasion of Quintus, Malya was a junior officer of the Quintus [[Planetary Defence Forces]]. She was amongst the few surviving [[Loyalist|loyal]] members of the PDF after Voldorius conquered the planet and soon became one of the senior members of the pro-Imperial resistance.{{Fn|1a}} She became aware of a [[Space Marine]] force operating on Qunitus and sought to make herself useful to them, transmitting whatever information she could to aid them.{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|1c}}

After [[Makaal|a member of Malya's resistance cell]] disobeyed her orders and led a failed assassination attempt on Voldorius, the Daemon Prince punished the inhabitants of Quintus by massacring the population of the city of [[Mankarra]].{{Fn|1a}} Although Malya was amongst the thousands gathered and brought to the city's main square, her life was spared and instead she was forced to serve Voldorius as his new [[equerry]].{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|1b}}

While serving as Voldorius's equerry, she continued to supply the Space Marines with intel on the weak points of Mankarra when they [[Hunt for Voldorius|made their move to liberate Quintus]]. However, Voldorius was aware of her treachery and forced her to serve as a new host for his greatest weapon, the [[Bloodtide]].{{Fn|1c}}{{Fn|1d}}

