'''Maraeus Orasus''' was a [[Salamanders]] [[Legionary]], who served in a [[Tactical Marine|tactical squad]] during the [[Great Crusade]] and the [[Horus Heresy]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
[[Image:MaraesusOrasus.jpeg|thumb|right|275px|Maraeus Orasus{{Fn|1}}]]
He was a [[Legionary]] for half a decade,{{Fn|2b}} when the [[Horus Heresy]] began and it caused Orasus to wonder what events had led to the [[Warmaster]]'s betrayal. When the [[Salamanders]]' forces took part in the first attack wave on [[Isstvan V]], Orasus' squadron was going to be deployed via a [[gunship]]. However, the aircraft was shot down before it could land and Orasus was the only survivor of the crash. Afterwards, the Legionary continued to follow his general orders and advanced upon [[Horus]]' '''Urgall Plateau''' '''Fortress'''.{{Fn|2a}} Like all of his [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]]'s forces, Orasus was charged with attacking the portion of the Fortress that was defended by the [[Death Guard]]. As he made his way to it, Orasus fought with rage and regret,{{Fn|2b}} at the [[Traitor Legions]]' betrayal, which created a future he never thought was possible.{{Fn|2a}} Though he was fighting by himself, the Legionary was able to kill several of the Death Guard, before he collapsed after being shot. But before Orasus could be killed by the Traitor Legion, he was saved by the Salamanders [[Saturnine Terminator]]s [[Tiamastus]] and [[Vort (Terminator)|Vort]].{{Fn|2b}}

After learning that Orasus was the only survivor of his squadron, [[Tiamastus]] ordered the [[Legionary]] to join them and the three continued to fight their way to the '''Fortress'''.{{Fn|2b}} They were able to meet up with other [[Salamanders]] near their objective, but the [[Death Guard]] soon launched a counter attack. However, the [[Traitor Legion]] used [[Phosphex]] canisters to disperse a mist to cover their advance. Shortly after the three Salamanders were engulfed by the mist, though, [[Tiamastus]] and [[Vort (Terminator)|Vort]] were suddenly [[Silence (Death Guard)|killed]] by the Death Guard's [[Primarch]], [[Mortarion]]. Orasus was then about to be the next to die, when the Salamanders' Primarch, [[Vulkan]], appeared and [[Dawnbringer|blocked]] his traitorous brother's blow.{{Fn|2c}}

With his life spared, Orasus continued to fight besides his fellow [[Salamanders]] against the [[Death Guard]]. As he did so, the [[Legionary]] constantly spoke a death chant, until the Salamanders received the order to disengage. This was so the [[Imperium]]'s second attack wave could take their place and Orasus joined the Salamanders marching towards their designated landing zone.{{Fn|2d}} When they neared it though, the [[Warmaster]] [[Horus]] ordered the [[Dropsite Massacre]] to begin and the Salamanders were attacked by the traitorous [[Iron Warriors]]. When Orasus came under fire he thought it was a case of mistaken identity, as the [[phosphex]] the Salamanders had fought through, had left his [[power armor]] grey. Orasus tried to warn the Iron Warriors of this, but before he could do so, the Traitor Legion fired once again.{{Fn|2e}} While Orasus survived the attack, the Legionary was later killed on [[Isstvan V]] by the [[Alpha Legion]].{{Fn|1}} 

