Marco Lillo.wikitext:
{{TanithPortal}}
'''Marco Lillo'''{{Fn|1a}} was a [[Verghast]]ite [[Guardsman]] of the [[Tanith First and Only]] [[Imperial Guard Regiment|regiment]].{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|2a}}


==Biography==
Lillo originally served in the [[Vervun Primary]], the [[PDF|standing army]] of [[Vervunhive]] on the planet Verghast. His twenty-one year career with the Vervun Primary came to an end following the [[Siege of Vervunhive]]; as Vervunhive had been reduced to a ruin over the course of the Siege, [[Warmaster]] [[Macaroth]] officially declared the [[hive]] dissolved but allowed any surviving Vervunhivers to [[Act of Consolation|enlist]] with the [[Imperial Guard]] and reinforce the regiments of the [[Sabbat Worlds Crusade]]. Lillo accepted the offer and was drafted into the Tanith First, the so-called "[[Ibram Gaunt|Gaunt's]] Ghosts".{{Fn|1a}}

He was amongst those new recruits to the regiment who saw its commanding officer, [[Colonel-Commissar]] [[Ibram Gaunt]], as a great hero (Gaunt, having taken charge of Vervunhive's defence towards the end of the Siege, had been responsible for the Imperial victory in the conflict, even if that victory had been Pyrrhic in nature).{{Fn|1a}} Gaunt himself considered Lillo to be one of the best of the Verghastite contingent of the regiment, on par with the likes of [[Agun Soric]].{{Fn|1b}}{{Fn|2b}}

Lillo first saw action with the Ghosts on [[Hagia]], fighting to retake the [[Holy Doctrinopolis]] from the [[Infardi]].{{Fn|1a}} He served under [[Sergeant (Imperial Guard)|Sergeant]] [[Haller]].{{Fn|2a}}

Later, Lillo joined the rest of his regiment in the [[Phantine (Planet)|Phantine]] theatre. Following the assault on the city of [[Cirenholm]], a combination of battlefield casualties and the pressing need to more fully integrate the Verghastite elements of the Tanith First led Colonel-Commissar Gaunt and [[Commissar]] [[Viktor Hark|Hark]] to put forward a number of Verghastite Troopers for consideration for promotion. Lillo was suggested for one of the positions by Hark, and Gaunt agreed that he would be a good choice.{{Fn|2b}}

