Marcus Valerius.wikitext:
{{ImperiumPortal}}
{{otheruses|USE=Vice-Caesari of the [[Therion Cohort]]|OTHERPAGE=Valerius (disambiguation)}}
[[Image:ValeriusArt.jpg|thumb|right|220px|{{PAGENAME}}{{Fn|4}}]]
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' was a [[Praefactor]] and later [[Vice-Caesari]] of the [[Imperial Army]] during the [[Great Crusade]] and [[Horus Heresy]].{{Fn|1}}

{{Spoiler|source=Deliverance Lost (Novel)}}
{{Spoiler|source=The Face of Treachery (Short Story)}}
Commanding the [[Therion Cohort]], shortly before the [[Drop Site Massacre]] Marcus' forces were stationed on the [[Raven Guard]] homeworld of [[Deliverance]]. During his stay on Deliverance Marcus began to become haunted by strange dreams that seemed to foretell [[Drop Site Massacre|catastrophe]] for the Raven Guard. Raven Guard commander [[Branne]] became suspicious that this was an omen, and eventually left for [[Isstvan V]] to see if their Primarch [[Corax]] was okay. When they arrived in-system, the Raven Guard had been massacred and Branne was able to save Corax himself.{{Fn|1}}{{fn|5}}

Later, Marcus led the [[Therion Cohort]] in the attack on the [[Perfect Fortress]].{{Fn|1}} However after having visions of [[Leman Russ (Primarch)|Leman Russ]] meeting his end at the hands of traitor forces, Valerius confided to [[Corax]] of the supernatural nature of his visions as well as his belief that it was the guidance of the [[Emperor]], whom he now worshiped as a god. This enraged [[Corax]], but he nonetheless followed Valerius's visions, resulting in the [[Raven Guard]] saving the [[Space Wolves]] in the [[Battle of Yarant]].{{Fn|2}}

Due to his beliefs, [[Corax]] banished Valerius from his sight. He eventually made his way to [[Beta-Garmon]], where he led the [[Therion Cohort]] against enemy [[Titan]]s in the [[Battle of Beta-Garmon]], which despite the sheer carnage, Valerius would ultimately survive.{{Fn|3}}

