Marduk Tamaris.wikitext:
{{SlaaneshPortal}}{{EmperorsChildrenPortal}}
'''Marduk Tamaris''' is the [[Chaos Lord|Knight-Commander]] of the [[Perfecti]] [[Chaos Warband|Warband]], in the [[Emperor's Children]]'s [[3rd Company (Emperor's Children)|3rd Company]].{{Fn|1a}} 
==History==
A [[Horus Heresy]] veteran and an oathsworn blademaster of his [[Daemon Primarch]] [[Fulgrim]], Tamaris wields the [[power sword]] [[Exquisite Blade]]. He is a skilled warrior, who improves with every battle and Tamaris aims to one day achieve perfection with his sword skills. As the [[Chaos Lord|Knight-Commander]] was leading the [[Perfecti]] against a [[World Eaters]] [[Chaos Warband|Warband]] in [[M42]], the [[Emperor's Children]] were summoned to their Primarch's side. The [[Sorcerer Lord]] [[Mauvais]] was tasked with delivering the summons to the Perfecti and appeared just as Tamaris seemingly killed the World Eaters' [[Chaos Lord|Warlord]], by using his Blade to impale the commander. However the Warlord grabbed hold of Tamaris' sword arm and pulled himself towards the Knight-Commander until they were mere inches away from each other. Tamaris was unable to break free of the Warlord's grasp, but the Knight-Commander was saved when Mauvais made his presence known by killing the World Eater. With that, the Perfecti were victorious though, Tamaris was left humiliated and did not thank Mauvais for his aid.{{Fn|1a}}

This annoyed the Sorcerer Lord, but Mauvais proceeded to tell Tamaris that Fulgrim was summoning the Emperor's Children to him, aboard the warship [[Vexation]]. Mauvais remarked, however, that it was up to Tamaris to attend the summons or not, as he doubted anyone would notice or care if the Knight-Commander showed up either way. With that, the Sorcerer Lord departed as Tamaris ordered the Perfecti to ready themselves to leave for the Vexation. While he was still humiliated by Mauvais' intervention, Tamaris' second in command, [[Venakhar]], reminded him of the opportunity Fulgrim's summon represented and that only the weak dwelled on the past. Tamaris agreed with this and vowed to look towards the perfection the future held for him.{{Fn|1a}} 

Tamaris becomes the primary Emperor's Children commander in the subsequent invasion of the world of [[Crucible (World)|Crucible]] alongside Mauvais. Tamaris is tasked by Fulgrim personally with killing the [[Johannes Berengar|Black Templars Emperor's Champion]] predicted to be on Crucible.{{Fn|1b}} After frustration at being denied a chance to kill [[Black Templars]] [[Castellan (Black Templars)|Castellan]] [[Garrian]] in battle,{{Fn|1c}} Tamaris is able to destroy the Imperial defenders water supply.{{Fn|1d}}

In the final battle to storm Crucible's Citadel, Tamaris engages in battle with Emperor's Champion Berengar. However he is blinded and about to be defeated by Berengar before Fulgrim himself intervenes and drives back the Emperor's Champion. Fulgrim and his retinue of warriors turn the tide, and Berengar is able to decapitate a wounded Berengar with his own [[Black Sword]].{{Fn|1e}}

After the battle, Tamaris accompanies Fulgrim to the victory ceremony in the Citadel. The crowd roars both their names, but Tamaris feels the victory is hollow and all their fighting and blood spilled had just been a game to their Primarch. Tamaris is declared Fulgrim's perfect son and personal champion, but the Emperor's Children warrior knows he will quickly be forgotten.{{Fn|1f}}

