Marek Angeloi.wikitext:
{{DeathwatchPortal}}
{{ScythesOfTheEmperorPortal}}
'''Marek Angeloi'''{{Fn|2}} was a [[Space Marine Sergeant|sergeant]] in the [[Scythes of the Emperor]] [[Chapter|Chapter's]] [[4th Company (Scythes of the Emperor)|Fourth Company]], around the time of the fall of [[Sotha]].{{Fn|1}}{{Fn|3a}}

He was [[Tiresias|Brother Tiresias's]] superior at the time that [[Chapter Master]] [[Thrasius]] returned from planning for the future of the Scythes after their near-destruction by [[Hive Fleet Kraken]]. Both Angeloi and Tiresias were openly critical of Thrasius's beliefs on the direction that the [[Chapter]] should take, and had rallied much support amongst their battle-brothers.{{Fn|1}}

Suddenly and without warning, Angeloi was sent away by [[Thrasius]] to join the [[Deathwatch]], along with more than forty other rebellious Scythes who had been identified as likely to speak out against their [[Chapter Master]]. This represented a loss of nearly a third of Chapter's fighting strength.{{Fn|1}}

[[Tiresias]] was shocked by Angeloi's departure, but was offered his own command as a [[Sergeant (Space Marines)|sergeant]] among the Salvation Teams instead of any other punishment.{{Fn|1}}

During his time in the Deathwatch, Angeloi fought many battles against the [[Tyranids]].{{Fn|2}} He was in command of a successful mission to purge the forested planet of [[Phirus]], and saved [[Felgir|one of his men]] from a [[Lictor]] during an ill-advised ritualised hunt. Following this mission, he requested to be returned to his parent chapter, but it is unknown whether this request was granted.{{Fn|2}}

==Wargear==
Angeloi carries a [[boltgun]] equipped with [[Stalker-pattern]] ammunition, and is a trained marksman.{{Fn|2}}{{Fn|3b}}

