Markus Castus.wikitext:
{{UltramarinesPortal}}
'''Markus Castus''' is an [[Ultramarines]] [[Primaris Lieutenant]] , who is considered a hero of his [[Chapter]].{{Fn|1b}}  
==History==
Driven by both a sense of duty and inflexible moral compass, Castus has become renowned as the victor of [[Varogan]], savior of [[Gathor's Landing]] and the slayer of Lord [[Kharag|Kharag the Bloody]]. The [[Primaris Lieutenant|Lieutenant]] also upholds the higher ideals eschewed by callous [[Imperial]] rulers and always seeks to do the right and just thing for [[Humanity]]{{Fn|1b}}. Unfortunately, his deeds drew the attention of the [[Necron Overlord]] [[Trazyn the Infinite]] and led the [[Xenos]] to kidnap Castus. He was then placed in an arena within the Overlord's hidden '''Sanctum''', which is connected to the [[Tomb World]] [[Solemnace]], via [[Reality-Tether]]s. Castus was not the only renowned warrior Trazyn had placed there and he soon faced the [[Blood Angel]] [[Rafelo]], the [[Death Guard]] [[Refulgus Grue]] and the [[Necron]] [[Teknoth]]. They were all brought there to fight for Trazyn's enjoyment, but the Overlord promised the victor would be freed from their imprisonment{{Fn|1a}}. Upon hearing this, Castus decided he would do whatever it took to return to the [[Ultramarines]] and warn them of what the Overlord had done. Even if that meant he would have to take the life of a fellow [[Space Marine]], now matter how repugnant the deed would be{{Fn|1b}}. However unbeknownst to Castus and the other warriors, Trazyn has no intention of freeing the arena winner. Instead the victor will have the honor of taking a place of pride within the Overlord's latest exhibit on Solemnace.{{Fn|1a}}   

==Sources==
