Martek Helm'ayr.wikitext:
{{NecromundaPortal}}
[[File:Martek Helm'ayr.jpg|300px|thumb|right|Martek Helm'ayr]]
'''Martek Helm'ayr''' was a [[Necromunda (planet)|Necromundan]] street tough from [[Hive Primus]] who led a war of conquest that finally ended the internal strife that had long plagued the [[Hive World]] since its [[Great Crusade|Compliance]].{{Fn|1a}} 

==Biography==
[[Tray’ayr Cyberia]], the final gang king to resist Imperial control on Necromunda, rejected the role of planetary governor imposed by the Imperium. He sought a return to the era of the [[Iron Lords (Araneus Continuity)|Iron Lords]], aiming for a Necromunda free from the heavy industrial demands enforced by the [[Emperor]]. Despite his defiance, Cyberia was not defeated by the Imperium itself but by Martek Helm’ayr, a powerful gang lord who emerged as a unifying force amidst Necromunda’s chaos. Helm’ayr made a solemn pledge to the [[Imperial Fists]], promising to unite Necromunda and uphold the [[Pax Imperium]]. Impressed by his dedication, [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Gaelos]] accepted his oath.{{Fn|1a}} 

Over a long and tumultuous conflict which took place between 012 and 085.[[M34]], Martek Helm’ayr brought the major hives under his control. Those that resisted were isolated and eventually compelled to swear allegiance to him. Before the century's end, Helm’ayr achieved his goal, fulfilling his oath to the Imperial Fists, ending Necromunda's unrest without further intervention from the Imperium.{{Fn|1b}} 

For his service, Martek was rewarded with becoming Necromunda's next [[Planetary Governor]]{{Fn|1b}} and he went on to establish a dynasty that became known as [[House Helm'ayr]], which ruled the [[Hive World]] for several millennia. Though the House was succeeded by its blood descendants of [[House Helmawr]]{{Fn|1c}}, Martek is still recognized as Helmawr's progenitor.{{Fn|1b}} 

==Legacy==
Several millennia after his death, however, Martek has become an enigmatic figure within the histories of Necromunda, as the records of his reign have been largely lost to history. Even his actual appearance is unknown, though grandiose statues and paintings of Martek's highly exaggerated physical depiction reside in the Spire of Hive Primus. It is rumored, though, that within the [[Imperial Fists]]' fortress atop Hive Primus, known as the [[Spear of Dorn]], there remains a fresco mural of one of the few remaining true images of Martek Helm'ayr, kneeling before an Imperial Fists [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]], as he takes the '''Oath of Governance'''.{{Fn|2}}

Necromunda's current [[Planetary Governor]], [[Gerontius Helmawr]], remembered Martek's features well though and in 995.[[M41]] he realized that one of his true-born sons looked like House Helmawr's ancient progenitor. Fearing that the blood of the usurper might flow in the child's veins, which would be greatly aided by having Martek's likeness, Gerontius made the decision to banish his son. However, the child was able to make his way down into [[Hive Primus|Hive Primus's]] [[Underhive]], where he was welcomed by a discarded line of his family and the dark masters they now followed.{{Fn|1d}}

