Maxillus.wikitext:
{{DeathwatchPortal}}
{{UltramarinesPortal}}
'''Maxillus''' is a [[Space Marine]] of the [[Deathwatch]], haling from the [[Ultramarines]] [[Chapter]].{{Fn|1}}


==Biograhpy==
At some point, Maxillus and [[Courlanth]] served on the same [[Kill-Team]]. They participated in a [[Gaunt (Tyranid)|Gaunt]] purge on the planet [[Masali]], exterminating one of the frequent resurgences of [[Tyranid]]s in the wake of the destruction of [[Hive Fleet]] [[Behemoth]].{{Fn|1}}

Maxillus was one of the Marines stationed at [[Watch Fortress]] [[Zarabek]] when it was discovered by the [[Ordo Xenos]] that [[human]] [[pirate]]s operating in the [[Teramus System]] somehow had access to functional [[Eldar]] [[lance]] weapons mounted on their ships. In a debate between the Marines present over the issue, [[Watch Captain]] [[Ska Mordentodt]] agreed to allow [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] [[Courlanth]] to assemble a kill-team and lead a mission into the Teramus system to uncover the source of the weapons and eliminate them; Maxillus was selected by Courlanth for the mission, partly because of the shared history between them.{{Fn|1}}

Courlanth led the Kill-Team in infiltrating the pirates' asteroid base and discovered that the pirate leader, [[Arlon Buke]], had entered into a pact with the [[Dark Eldar]] of the [[Kabal of the Crimson Blossom]]. When he saw that the pirates were trading captured slaves to the xenos in exchange for weapons and drugs, Courlanth abandoned stealth and ordered an attack on the Kabal and the pirates alike. In the resulting battle, Maxillus was killed by the Dark Eldar's poisoned [[Splinter Weaponry|splinter weapons]].{{Fn|1}}

==Wargear==
Maxillus was armed with a [[Boltgun|Crusade-pattern bolter]].{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[The Alien Hunters (Short Story)]] — [[Xenos Hunters (Anthology)]]

