Melissima Artos-Septus Iota.wikitext:
{{AdeptusMechanicusPortal}}
'''Melissima Artos-Septus Iota''' is an [[Adeptus Mechanicus]] [[Martian]] [[Skitarii Marshal]]. She serves as the de facto commander of [[Magos Dominus|Archmagos Dominus]] [[Belisarius Cawl]]'s military forces, aboard the [[Ark Mechanicus]] [[Zar-Quaesitor]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
Though gender is irrelevant for many of the [[Adeptus Mechanicus]], Iota revels in her femininity. The [[Skitarii Marshal|Marshal]]'s sculpted body is a tall, silver, armored and idolized version of her original form, with Iota's flesh having been pared back to the mere essentials. She only wears a red [[Martian]] cloak and is otherwise plated in an advanced [[adamantine]] corpus metallica, so that the Marshal appears to be entirely mechanical. This also includes her face, which is made of flexible metal, and can move as much as any [[human]]'s. However Iota mostly wears an expression of superior amusement on hers.{{Fn|1}} 

As [[Magos Dominus|Archmagos Dominus]] [[Belisarius Cawl]]'s commander, Iota has earned lots of glory fighting his battles and defending him from his foes. Despite her ranking, though, the [[Skitarii Marshal|Marshal]] has a strained relationship with the [[Primaris Space Marine]] [[Alpha Primus (Space Marine)|Alpha Primus]], who serves as Cawl's second-in-command. While the Marshal is cordial with Primus, the Primaris is often rude to Iota and he attempts to supersede her authority with the Dominus' forces. This is due to Primus believing he has a close relationship with Cawl, as the first successful Primaris Space Marine that the Dominus created. It is because of this, that Primus also gets irritated and angry, when Iota criticizes Cawl in anyway, as the Primaris thinks that only he has the right to do so. It does not help matters, that Cawl lets them both believe that their status with him is correct.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Genefather (Novel)]], Chapter 12 
