Meryn.wikitext:
{{TanithPortal}}
'''Meryn''' was a [[Guardsman]] of the [[Tanith First and Only]] [[Imperial Guard Regiment|regiment]] (also known as ''"[[Ibram Gaunt|Gaunt's]] Ghosts"'').{{Fn|1}}{{Fn|2a}}{{Fn|4}}


==Biography==
===Early Career===
Meryn was one of the original [[Tanith]] members of the regiment, holding the rank of [[Corporal]] when the Tanith First was founded.{{Fn|2a}}{{Fn|3}} He was one of the younger Tanith Guardsmen, but was regarded as reliable nonetheless.{{Fn|5c}}

In the [[Sabbat Worlds Crusade]]'s assault on [[Caligula (Hive World)|Caligula]], Meryn was on a [[troop-ship]] which was shot down by a [[Psyker|psychic storm]] over [[Nero Hive]]. Thanks to the leadership of [[Colonel-Commissar]] [[Ibram Gaunt]], the survivors of the crash managed to make it off Caligula and reunite with the rest of the Crusade.{{Fn|2b}} He was later part of a Tanith detachment assigned to escort a supply convoy from [[Aurelian Hive]] to [[Hive Calphernia]], driving a [[track-bike]] with [[Trooper]] [[Dermon Caffran|Caffran]] manning the [[Autocannon|guns]].{{Fn|2c}}

By the time of the [[Menazoid Epsilon]] campaign, Meryn led one of the [[Imperial Guard Regiment|regiment's]] [[platoon]]s.{{Fn|1}}

When the Tanith First were deployed to reinforce [[Vervunhive]] as it was [[Siege of Vervunhive|under siege]] by the [[Ferrozoica]]ns, Meryn was one of the defenders of the [[Hass East Fort]], serving under [[Sergeant (Imperial Guard)|Sergeant]] [[Ceglan Varl|Varl]].{{Fn|3}}

===Post-Verghast===
At some point following the Siege of Vervunhive, Meryn had been taken under the wing of [[Major]] [[Elim Rawne|Rawne]]. A number of the Ghosts noted that Meryn had changed as a result of Rawne's mentorship, with Meryn becoming far more ruthless.{{Fn|5c}}

In '''771.[[M41]]''', as part of the Tanith deployment on [[Phantine (Planet)|Phantine]], Meryn was selected personally by Colonel-Commissar Gaunt to take part in [[Operation Larisel]]{{Fn|5a}}, commanding the operation's second team.{{Fn|5b}}{{Fn|5c}}


==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
===Conflicting sources===
It is unclear when exactly Meryn was promoted from [[Corporal]] to [[Sergeant (Imperial Guard)|Sergeant]]: he is first referred to as Sergeant in the novel ''[[Honour Guard (Novel)|Honour Guard]]''.{{Fn|4}} However, [[The Guns of Tanith (Novel)|the following book]] in the [[Gaunt's Ghosts (Novel Series)|Gaunt's Ghosts novel series]], he is stated at different points to be a Corporal{{Fn|5a}}{{Fn|5c}} or Sergeant{{Fn|5c}} (notably it swaps in the same section).{{Fn|5c}}

