Messelina.wikitext:
{{EcclesiarchyPortal}}
'''Messelina''' was an [[Imperial Saint]] that is celebrated and held in high regard across the [[Moebian Domain]] to this day.{{Fn|3a}}

{{clear}}
==Biography==
At an unspecified point in the Moebian Domain's history, a girl named Messelina would gather a significant following in her zealous pursuit of [[heretic]]s and the liberation of many worlds in the Moebian Domain. She and her followers liberated many Moebian worlds through blood and fire, and said to have brought on an age of peace to the domain.{{Fn|3}}

Messelina was a devout follower of the [[Imperial Creed]] and would attempt to dissuade any worship or excessive praise of herself. Many hymns would be written of her during her time, but she rejected all of them, for she feared she would become a subject of idolatry. Many more hymns, shrines, and grand cathedrals would be raised in her name after her death.{{Fn|2f}}

Her followers are noted as having liberated [[Arvania City]] and a [[combat sword]] belonging to one of these followers would go on to become a revered relic held by the [[Shrine of Saint Messelina in Purity]].{{Fn|2c}} At some point, Messelina is said to have beheaded the corrupt rulers of one of [[Branx Magna|Branx]]'s moons. This would later be remembered and celebrated in the Moebian Domain as [[Severance Day]].{{Fn|4}}

Millennia ago, great factorums in [[Hive Tertium]] were built to supply Saint Messelina's crusade through the Moebian Domain. These facilities were known as [[Machinaria Gloriana]]. Each is rumoured to house some technological marvel that significantly aided the war effort. One of these long-forgotten wonders have been recently rediscovered in [[M42]]. Atelium Foundryplex Omega V, also known as [[Clandestium Gloriana]], is a facility that can produce [[Moebian Steel]].{{Fn|5}}

She would eventually be betrayed by members of the [[Imperial Creed]],{{Fn|3a}} likely leading to her death. A group of her followers hunted down these betrayers and went on to form the [[Cult of Sanguine Reprisal]]. The cult continues to operate in the [[Moebian Fringe]] to this day,{{Fn|2a}} millennia after Messelina's death.{{Fn|5}}

==Overview==
Saint Messelina's opinions of psykers are a contentious subject in the present day [[M42]]. [[Historitor]]s argue about her attitude to [[Psyker]]s, while the keepers of her shrines insist she abhorred them.{{Fn|2e}} Something rarely brought up amongst the zealous, if acknowledged at all about Messelina, was that she herself was a psyker.{{Fn|3b}}

It is said that Messelina witnessed the fall of [[Komaris]], the Imperial bastion of the Moebian Fringe, and shed tears when witnessing its fall. A moon near Komaris, [[Messelina Gloriana]], would become a minor [[Shrine World]] bearing her namesake. Many shrines dedicated to her would be built on the world.{{Fn|1}}{{Fn|2b}}

There is no mention of [[Ogryn]]s in [[Caladoc]]'s "[[Life of Saint Messelina]]". Some think this might indicate that the vat-grown strain of Ogryn had not yet been introduced to the [[Moebian Domain]] during Messelina's lifetime.{{Fn|2g}}

===Teachings===
The purported teachings of Messelina revolve around merciless killing through righteous fury,{{Fn|2j}} judicious application of violence,{{Fn|2n}} and purifying flame.{{Fn|2h}}{{Fn|2i}}

Some zealots believe they can hear Messelina when in prayer. These devout individuals believe she speaks to them saying "''Burn them''" and "''Make them unto ashes in my name.''"{{Fn|2h}} Many sects that venerate Saint Messelina believe in the purifying powers of flame, especially in the case of purifying [[heretic]]s.{{Fn|2i}} [[Hexorcist]]s are very much in line with Messelina's teachings.{{Fn|2j}} Many adherents to the teaching of Saint Messelina carry a set of delicate Prayer Chimes with them.{{Fn|2k}}

