Metaurus.wikitext:
{{QuoteBox|
quote=''"Humans are born prey. Fragile. Afraid. The Imperium selects a chosen few. Children we break over decades of conditioning. Purging them of weakness. Carving out their fear. Those that survive are reborn with the strength to level cities, to conquer worlds. But power must be controlled. Fear forged into obedience. Into faith.''<br><br>
''Centuries ago, I chose a child filled with pain and rage. A child who had never known fear. What could a soul like that be capable of?"''{{Fn|1}}}}
{{UltramarinesPortal}}
[[Image:Metaurus.jpg|thumb|right|240px|Metaurus{{Fn|1}}]]
'''Metaurus''' is an [[Ultramarines]] [[Bladeguard Veteran]] [[Veteran Sergeant|Sergeant]], who was once a [[Firstborn]] before he underwent the [[Rubicon Primaris]].{{Fn|1}}

==Biography==
The [[Veteran Sergeant|Sergeant]] was the one who discovered and chose a young [[Demetrian Titus]] to become an [[Aspirant]] for the [[Ultramarines]]. He found young Titus on a battlefield carrying an [[Astartes Combat Knife]].{{Fn|2}} Metaurus describes Titus as having only known rage and pain as a child, but not fear, and worries what a soul like that might be capable of becoming.{{Fn|1}}

===Mission to Zsah’Uj===
More than two centuries later, the two would undergo a mission together, sometime after Titus was reinstated into the [[Chapter]] as a [[Primaris Lieutenant]].{{Fn|1}}

Metaurus would lead a small squad of Ultramarines on this mission. Taking place on the world [[Zsah’Uj]], the primary objective was to locate and destroy an apostate relic, an idol to the [[Chaos God]] [[Tzeentch]]. Secondary objective was to secure ordinance strike coordinates. Besides Titus, Metarus's squad also included two [[Bladeguard Veteran]]s, [[Icaron]] and [[Levantus]]. The squad was launched from a [[Strike Cruiser|strike cruiser]] via a [[drop pod]], which would fire upon the idol's approximate location. Warp influence in the area causes ordinance targeting arrays and communications systems to not function. Thus the need for a strike team to destroy the idol and [[Sorcerer]] leading the cult.{{Fn|1}}

Upon landing, Metaurus' squadron fought through numerous Tzeentch [[Cultist]]s and [[Tzaangors]] as they proceeded towards the idol. After cutting a bloody swath through the cult's forces they reached their target, a large statue of a [[Greater Daemon]] known as a [[Lord of Change]]. They would deploy a portable device that functioned similar to a [[Gellar Field]], a casket containing an [[Astropath]] and the portable Gellar Field tech.{{Fn|2}}

While the squad unleashed a volley of bolter fire on the idol, they were attacked by a the High Priestess of the Tzeentchian cult, who was hidden in the orb of the idol's staff prior to their arrival. The highly gifted Sorceress used her powers to freeze them in place, after disabling their defences by throwing  knife through the Astropath's heart.{{Fn|2}} The now-vulnerable Space Marines could do nothing against her Warp magics. The Sorceress entered their minds of each Marine, killing them one by one. She would first kill Icaron and Levantus.{{Fn|1}}

When the Sorceress entered the mind of Metaurus, the vision she evoked that of the child he chose ''"a child who has never known fear"'', as she said to him. The vision was of Metaurus observing Demetrian Titus, first as a child, then a Space Marine, then a [[Chaos Space Marine]]. The Chaos Space Marine form of Titus in the vision would then gut Metarus with a knife.{{Fn|1}} Metaurus was left severely wounded. He sustained a series of serious internal injuries: critical failure of his [[Larraman's Organ]], [[Belisarian Furnace]] unresponsive, [[Oolitic Kidney|Oolitic systems]] inactive, and [[Creation of a Space Marine#Sus-an Membrane|Sus-an membrane]]: primed. Along with this, his armour was no longer  fully sealed or void-capable as soon as he was stabbed.{{Fn|2}}

When the Sorcereress entered the mind of Titus, however, the Lieutenant was able to break free of its control. Having shattered the Sorcerer's staff in his vision she attempted to take flight, but Titus quickly killed her before she could escape. Titus provided coordinates for ordinance and pulled the wounded Metaurus to safety. Back at the ravine's entrance, they hordes of cultists came flooding from the distance at one end of the chasm. Titus placed Metaurus against a rock while preparing to defend against the apostate tide.{{Fn|1}}

===Present===
Metaurus is currently part of Demetrian Titus' [[Command Squad]] within the [[2nd Company (Ultramarines)|Ultramarines 2nd Company]].{{Fn|3}}

