{{Spoiler|source=The Bleeding Chalice (Novel)}}

'''Michairas''' was a [[Space Marine]] of the [[Soul Drinkers]] [[Chapter]].{{Fn|1a}}

While a [[Space Marine Scout|novice]] of the Chapter, Michairas served as an [[equerry]] to [[Space Marine Commander|Commander]] [[Caeon]] for some years before he was elevated to a [[Brother|Battle-Brother]].  As a result, when Caeon was dying of poisoning on the [[Van Skorvold Star Fort]] after being stabbed by [[Veritas Van Skorvold]], Michairas was one of the Marines called upon to undertake Caeon's last rites.{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|1b}}

Command of operations aboard the star fort fell to Caeon's named successor, [[Sarpedon]].{{Fn|1a}}  However, Sarpedon would end up leading most of the Chapter in [[Renegade Chapter|rebellion]] against the [[Imperium]].  Michairas was one of the [[Space Marines|Marines]] who tried to fight back against Sarpedon and his supporters, but was unsuccessful; as Michairas tried to lead a band of novices to flee aboard the ''[[Glory]]'', he was thrown out of an airlock by Sarpedon himself and presumed dead.{{Fn|1c}}

To Sarpedon's surprise, however, Michairas survived this incident.  He would eventually serve in the retinue of [[Inquisitor]] [[Thaddeus (Inquisitor)|Thaddeus]] of the [[Ordo Hereticus]], aiding him in tracking down his renegade former brothers.  He was killed fighting against Sarpedon on [[Stratix Luminae]].{{Fn|2}}

