'''{{PAGENAME}}''' is the current [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] of the [[Ultramarines]] [[3rd Company (Ultramarines)|3rd Company]] and [[Master of the Arsenal]].{{Fn|1}}

===Biography===
It was 3rd Company Captain [[Ardias]] who first honoured his warriors by taking the company’s heraldic colour and working it into his personal heraldry. This tradition has been maintained ever since, with Captain Mikael Fabian proving no exception. Fabian is a hard-headed and stubborn warrior whose xenophobic hatred is so pronounced that it knows few equals, even amongst the alien-hunting specialists of the [[Ordo Xenos]], and a direct man who prefers thorough and straightforward solutions. He is more than happy to unleash overwhelming force in order to make absolutely sure that an alien infestation has been eradicated, and favours the deployment of [[flamer]] weaponry, [[Land Raider Redeemer]]s and copious [[hellfire round]]s. For all his stern intractability, Captain Fabian expects all of his warriors to be forthright with him in sharing their strategic appraisal of the developing battlefield situation, and has been known to shift plans on the advice of a single well-placed battle-brother.{{Fn|7}}

Shortly before the [[Siege of Zalathras]] Fabian was leading 3rd company, and the Deo Volante fleet, against traitor forces in the systems beyond [[Iax]]. He was confident that with the guard divisions assigned to him he could mop up resistance on the cleansed worlds, and still proceed with an offensive on schedule.{{Fn|8}}

In the aftermath of the [[Bloodborn]]'s failed [[Invasion of Ultramar]], Fabian was overseeing the resupply of his forces on [[Macragge]] as they prepared to depart on the warship ''[[Accipiter (Strike Cruiser)|Accipiter]]''. When their rearmament was nearly done, Fabian boarded a [[Thunderhawk]] to take him back to the warship, but disaster struck when it neared the orbital '''Lysis Macar''' littoral platform. At that exact moment, a group of surviving Bloodborn [[Cultists]] activated an atomic bomb that destroyed the littoral platform and the electromagnetic pulse  from the explosion hit dozens of aircraft near the Lysis Macar. The pulse made the aircrafts' avionics and engine controls short out, which caused the uncontrollable aircraft to hurtle towards the ground. Fabian's Thunderhawk was among them and it shattered to pieces when it hit one of Macragge's oceans.{{Fn|2}}

However, he survived the crash and was later present on the world of Sycorax, along with [[Uriel Ventris]] as the 3rd and [[4th Company (Ultramarines)|4th]] companies of the Ultramarines defended the world from a virulent [[Ork]] infestation.{{Fn|5}}

Sometime later the Captain joined the [[Indomitus Crusade]] and led his Company to battle against the forces of [[Chaos]] in the [[Koryndil Reach]]. Due to the effects of the [[Great Rift]]'s creation, communication between the Crusade's far flung forces was difficult, but its leadership later received a message of ill tidings from Fabian. Composed of only a single sentence, it stated that the Third had suffered a great defeat and afterwards the Indomitus Crusade received no further contact from the Captain.{{Fn|6}}

