Mohana Mankata VI.wikitext:
{{CollegiaTitanicaPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''', known to her subordinates as '''Great Mother''', was the commanding [[Princeps]] of the [[Legio Solaria]] during the [[Great Crusade]] and [[Horus Heresy]].{{Fn|1a}}

==History==
Born on the [[Knight World]] of [[Procon (Knight World)|Procon]], Mohana was denied the right to pilot a [[Knight]] in [[House Procon Vi]] due to her gender. However when the [[Great Crusade]] arrived at Procon, a horseback riding contest was held for the visiting [[Imperial]] delegation. Defying her father's wishes, Mohana appeared at the contest on horseback and won the contest, impressing the [[Mechanicum]] delegates. Though she was exiled for the act, she managed to secure Mechanicum support and became the founding member of a new [[Titan Legion]], the [[Legio Solaria]]. Serving as the Princeps of the [[Warlord Titan]] ''[[Luxor Invictoria]]'', Mohana made the Legio Solaria into a force of all-women which paid tribute to the Procon goddess of the hunt Pahkmetris, with whatever men that were recruited trained as [[Tech-Priest]]s or converted [[Servitor]]s. The Legion served well throughout the Great Crusade, becoming known for hit-and-run tactics.{{Fn|1a}}

In the subsequent [[Schism of Mars]] Mohana remained loyal to the [[Imperium]] but by the end of the [[Horus Heresy]] had grown so old that she could no longer survive outside of a life support capsule aboard the ''Luxor Invictoria''. Little more than few weeks life left were estimated for her by the time of the [[Battle of Beta-Garmon]], where she commanded the Legio Solaria. During the battle on [[Beta-Garmon II]], the ''Luxor Invictoria'' was badly damaged by the debris shower caused by the destruction of an orbiting [[Starfort]]. Mohana was recovered from the wreckage but died shortly after surrounded by her surrogate daughters.{{Fn|1b}}

