Mont'ka Mese'Ukos.wikitext:
{{TauPortal}}
'''Mont'ka Mese'Ukos''' was once a [[Tau Commander|Commander]] in the [[T'au Empire]], where he had previously served under [[Commander Farsight]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
Just like [[Farsight]], though, Mese'Ukos has also diverged from the ways of the [[T'au Empire]] and rebelled against it. This occurred, when he was among{{Fn|1}} the T'au's [[Third Sphere of Expansion]] forces{{Fn|2}} that invaded the [[Imperial]] [[Sector]]s near the [[Damocles Gulf]], in the wake of the [[13th Black Crusade]]. As the Empire sought to increase its territories,{{Fn|3}} however, the [[Tau Commander|Commander]] and his forces struck out on their own. He followed in Farsight's footsteps by establishing his own Enclave, which Mese'Ukos then sought to expand at all costs.{{Fn|1}} The Imperium later launched the [[Dark Crusade (Imperium)|Dark Crusade]]'s [[Mont'shi Campaign]] against the invading [[Xenos]], though,{{Fn|3}} and the Commander would become one of its priority targets. Deemed a dangerous threat, because not even the T'au Empire could control him, Mese'Ukos was then forced to fight against the Imperium, [[Orks]] and his former brethren.{{Fn|1}} In the end, however, the Mont'shi Campaign's Imperial forces were defeated by the T'au{{Fn|3}} and Mese'Ukos and his Enclave survived the conflict.{{Fn|1}}
