Mont'shi.wikitext:
{{TauPortal}}
'''Aun'o Mont'shi''' is a [[Vash'ya]] [[Sept]] [[Ethereal]] in the [[T'au Empire]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
As part of its [[Third Sphere of Expansion]],{{Fn|2}} Mont'shi commanded the [[T'au Empire]]'s invasion of the [[Imperial]] [[Sectors]] that were closest to the [[Damocles Gulf]], in the wake of the [[Thirteenth Black Crusade]]. He was assisted in this by the [[Tau Commander|Commander]] [[Eirl'O'Vash]] and was given ample support as the invasion was ordered by the Empire's [[Ethereal]]s. However the Imperium would later launch the [[Dark Crusade (Imperium)|Dark Crusade]]'s [[Mont'shi Campaign]] against the invading the [[Xenos]].{{Fn|1}} The Campaign was named after Mont'shi himself, as the Imperium had determined that the Ethereal was the leader of the T'au's invasion and was a major threat to it.{{Fn|3}} 

During the course of the [[Mont'shi Campaign]], the [[Imperial]] world [[Draven III]] and the [[Vendrea System]], were targeted by the [[T'au Empire]], with Vendrea being of particular interest to the [[Ethereal]] Mont'shi. He sent [[Tau Pathfinder|scouts]] there to locate a structure he knew was important to the T'au's future and after it was found, Mont'shi ordered its location to be secured from the Imperium's hands at once. This responsibility fell to the [[Water Caste]] emissary [[Ori'priam]], who had delivered the news of the structure's location to the Ethereal. Mont'shi also gave the Emissary orders to deliver to [[Tau Commander|Commander]] [[Eirl'O'Vash]], that would counter the Imperial reinforcements that were being sent to Draven III, which Ori'priam had also informed him of.{{Fn|3}} Sometime later, the Mont'shi Campaign was defeated by the T'au Empire, though the Imperium would continue to send its forces there in order to stop the Xenos' advancement into its territory.{{Fn|1}} Mont'shi would use the Campaign's failure and the subsequent [[The Fall of Medusa V|war]] on [[Medusa V]] to mask his actions and also sent the T'au Empire's forces to the embattled Imperial world. Chief among them were [[Earth Caste]] scientists, who were charged with studying the [[Warp Storm]] that was approaching Medusa V. It was hoped that by doing so, the scientists would gain the knowlege they needed to create [[Warp]] capable craft for the T'au Empire.{{Fn|4}}  

