Mordechai Ryken.wikitext:
{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
'''Mordechai Ryken'''{{Fn|1a}} was an officer of the [[Armageddon 101st Steel Legion]] [[Imperial Guard Regiment|Regiment]].{{Fn|1b}}{{Fn|1c}}

At the outbreak of the [[Third War for Armageddon]], Ryken held the rank of [[Major]] and acted as the second-in-command of the 101st Steel Legion under [[Colonel]] [[Sarren]].{{Fn|1b}}{{Fn|1c}} He was noted by Adjutant Quintus [[Cyria Tyro]] as being critical of the decision to abandon [[Hades Hive]] to [[Ork|the enemy]] in favour of reinforcing the other [[Hive]]s of [[Armageddon]].{{Fn|1b}}

Nevertheless, he complied with his orders to redeploy the 101st Steel Legion to [[Hive Helsreach]].{{Fn|1b}} He was a major figure in the defence of Helsreach, coordinating with [[Reclusiarch]] [[Merek Grimaldus]], commanding officer of the [[Black Templars]] of the [[Helsreach Crusade]].{{Fn|1c}} Towards the end of the siege of Helsreach, Ryken was amongst those of the 101st who, cut off from the main body of the regiment, decided to rally to the Templars' defence of the [[Temple of the Emperor Ascendant]].{{Fn|1d}}

In the aftermath of the siege of Helsreach, Ryken was one of the few survivors of the 101st. As a result, he was promoted to the rank of [[Colonel]].{{Fn|1e}}

