Morghana Nathrax.wikitext:
{{DarkEldarPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' is the ruling [[Dark Eldar]] [[Succubus]] of the [[Wych]] [[Cult of the Thirteenth Night]].{{Fn|1a}}

==History==

As a youth, Morghana was raised alongside [[Lelith Hesperax]] under the cruel [[Haemonculus]] [[Yukor]]. After their training was complete, the two parted ways to forge their own destiny's within [[Commorragh]]. While Lelith was fighting under the [[Ynnari]], Morghana overthrew her Succubus [[Ariex Sylene]] to become the new leader of the Cult of the Thirteenth Night.{{Fn|1a}} 

Upon Lelith's return to Commorragh, she discovered that [[Asdrubael Vect]] was now Morghana's patron and was supporting the Thirteenth Night against her own [[Cult of Strife]].{{Fn|1b}} In the end, Lelith was issued a duel challenge by Morghana in Vect's personal auditorium for the title of Queen of the Dark City.{{Fn|1c}} During the subsequent duel, with Vect in attendance, Lelith lost her weapon and Morghana offered her a chance to surrender. However Vect instead ordered Lelith's execution, causing an angry Morghana to unite against Vect. Lelith confronts Vect directly, taking his hand off at the wrist and demanding he cease his shadow war against her. Vect agreed, but subtly warned Lelith against publicly challenging his authority.{{Fn|1d}} Afterwards, Lelith entered a romantic relationship with Morghana and the two agreed to an uneasy alliance.{{Fn|1e}}

