Mrytun Dammergot.wikitext:
{{LOVPortal}}
'''Myrtun Dammergot''' is a [[Leagues of Votann]] [[Kin (Leagues of Votann)|Kin]] of the [[Trans-Hyperian Alliance]]'s [[Kindred of the Eternal Starforge]]. She served as [[Hernkyn Prospect]] [[Kâhl|Hernkâhl]]{{Fn|2g}} and commander of the ship, [[Grand Endeavour]]{{Fn|2a}}, before being promoted to the Kindred's [[Kâhl|High Kâhl]].{{Fn|2b}}

She is known to be especially old for a [[Kin (Leagues of Votann)|Kin]], enough that she is considered by the Kindred's [[Grimnyr|Lord Grimnyr]] to be a Living Ancestor.{{Fn|2e}} Her exact age is unknown, though she is noted as having spent over one hundred "orbits" away from her Kindred's [[Hold Ship]].{{Fn|2a}}

Myrtun enjoys assembling small dancing automata, using her time working on the constructs to think.{{Fn|2c}}

==History==
Though the [[Leagues of Votann]] are in a new age of conflict with the [[Imperium]], Dammergot has flourished by exploiting their battles for her own personal gain.{{Fn|1}} 

{{Spoiler|source=The High Kâhl's Oath (Novel)}}
Myrtun's first mission as a Hernkyn resulted in a massacre at the hands of the [[Orks]], of which she was one of the only survivors, leading her to carry a large amount of guilt. Her Grimnyr, [[Jôrdiki]], considers her to have become a "doom-seeker" as a result.{{Fn|2e}}

Myrtun led her prospect on a mission to attack, disable, and harvest a [[Tyranid]] [[Bioship]]; which went mostly to plan, until the arrival of fellow [[Kâhl|Hernkâhl]] [[Fyrtor]] and his ship the [[Canny Wanderer]].{{Fn|2a}} Refusing to stop her operation to speak with him, Fyrtor joins her aboard the Tyranid organism, where they defeat a [[Hive Tyrant|Node Lord]], with the help of a targeted laser blast directed by her most trusted companion, the [[Ironkin]] [[Wayfinder]] [[Lutar]]; and Fyrtor is finally able to inform her that she has been promoted to High Kâhl on recommendation from the three Trans-Hyperian [[Votann]] and the [[Votannic Council]].{{Fn|2b}}

Seeking to delay the responsibility, Myrtun avoids returning to the [[Kindred of the Eternal Starforge]]'s [[Hold Ship]], the [[Unbreakable Giant]], by performing mercenary work for some local [[Imperium of Man|Imperials]], leaving the actual harvesting of the Bioship to the local [[Urani-Surtr Regulates]] kindred.{{Fn|2c}}

Finally arriving at the Eternal Starforge Hold Ship, Myrtun takes a motorcade from the hangar to attend her first [[Hearthspake]] meeting as High Kâhl, before hearing petitions from the general populace. The first petitioner, a [[Brôkhyr]] Iron-Master named [[Lekki]] of the Enduring Guild of Master Runewrights, is interrupted by the [[Einhyr Champion]] Dori "Ironhelm" Hûltvan, who relays the oath sworn by Myrtun's predecessor, the deceased High Kâhl Orthônar, who was slain by [[Orks]] after rediscovering a Lost [[Hold]].{{Fn|2d}}

Despite some opposition within the [[Hearthspake]], Myrtun ultimately decides to follow after Orthônar and complete his oath.{{Fn|2e}} She sets off for the [[Oathstar]] system, only accessible through the [[Warp Storm]] known as the Well of Yrdu, accompanied by Lutar, Fyrtor, Dori, Jôrdiki, Chief Voidmaster Kyr Starbound, and the warships ''Grand Endeavour'', ''Canny Wanderer'', ''Hammer of Nithroggir'', and ''THA-C342''. The last vessel is lost in the [[Warp]], while the other ships, especially ''Canny Wanderer'', take damage engaging [[Chaos]] forces, but the fleet eventually arrive at their destination.{{Fn|2f}}

Receiving a message that the ''Unbreakable Giant'' has come under attack in their absence, Myrtun calls her council to Weigh the Decision of whether they should continue their mission, or return home. After a lengthy debate, they decide to press on and fulfill Orthônar's oath.{{Fn|2g}}

Battling the [[Orks]] which have occupied the lost Hold in the Kin's absence, Lutar is severely damaged battling the [[Warboss]], prompting Myrtun to attack it in a rage, destroying the ork's leg with her [[Volkanite Disintegrator]] and enabling Dori to finish the alien off. The Kin are able to fully reactivate the Hold's [[Fane]], which they use to locate a map to the lost Kindred's ancient [[Votann]], believed to be one of the original cores dating back to the oldest history of the Leagues. Once Lutar is repaired, Myrtun informs him that she will be leading the entire Kindred as High Kâhl in search of the Votann.{{Fn|2h}}

