Murgeist.wikitext:
{{DeathGuardPortal}}
'''Murgeist''' was a veteran [[Death Guard]] [[Terminator Sergeant]], who was among the [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]]'s forces that defended their [[Homeworld]], [[Barbarus]], when it was [[Siege of Barbarus|invaded]] during the [[Horus Heresy]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
He was subsequently under the command of [[Praetor (Rank)|Castellan-Praetor]] [[Vrokhorn]] on the '''Plains of Orthrya''', as the [[Loyalist]]s attacked it. As the battle commenced, the resolve of Vrokhorn's [[Death Guard]] was shaken, as the found themselves facing the wrath of the [[Primarch]]s [[El'Jonson]] and [[Russ]]. When [[Russ]] then led his [[Terminator]] escort upon Vrokhorn's position, Murgeist and the other Death Guard would not move. Vrokhorn, knew that such hesitation could cost them their opportunity to retaliate against the [[Space Wolves]] and he decided to charge at the Primarch. This broke the Death Guard's indecision and they quickly followed him to meet the Russ head on. The two forces then clashed and though the Praetor was cut down by the Primarch, the Death Guard were able to kill every single one of his escort. However even being alone, Russ was a powerful foe and he cut through the Death Guard. With Praetor fallen and the Space Wolves' Primarch beginning to overwhelm them, it was Murgeist who gave the order to retreat. Dragging the still living Vrokhorn with them, the Death Guard were able to escape, due to Russ waiting for more of his forces to reach him. When they did, though, the Primarch began to charge at the retreating Death Guard. The Space Wolves soon reached them and the Murgeist and the other Death Guard were slain by them. A badly wounded Vrokhorn, however, was able to reach the relative safety of the nearby '''Orthrya Bastion''', before his forces were destroyed.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[White Dwarf 481]], pgs. 119-120 - ''The Fate of Barbarus Part 2''

