Myrin Stormdawn.wikitext:
{{EldarPortal}}
'''Myrin Stormdawn''', is a [[Corsair Baron]] in the [[Starsplinters]] and former [[Admiral]] of the [[Craftworld]] [[Ilmaren]].{{Fn|1}} Myrin maintains a base within the [[Well of the Long Death]], a hollow planetoid within which a [[Waygate]] large enough to launch fleets from is found. Myrin wields a [[Void Sabre]],{{Fn|2a}} smells of woodsmoke and pine resin with purple-black hair,{{Fn|2c}} and routinely purchases items for far greater than their value simply to be ostentatious.{{Fn|2d}}

==History==
Formerly an [[Admiral]] of the [[Craftworld]] [[Ilmaren]], Stormdawn left the Craftworld after a disagreement with [[Farseer]] [[Caman]] of the Craftworld's [[Seer Council]] and brought with him nearly half of the Craftworld's fleet eventually finding a new home as a [[Corsair Baron]] in [[Corsair Princess|Princess]] [[Tishria]]'s [[Starsplinter]]s.{{Fn|2b}} In this role he famously defeated the [[Szarekh]] [[Necron Fleet|Dynastic Fleet]] at the [[Helmingvar Shipyard]]s and navigated [[Chaos Space Marine]]s devoted the [[Abaddon the Despoiler|The Despoiler]] into a black hole.{{fn|2b}}

He has been forced to enter into an alliance with the exiled [[Admiral]] [[Taenar Leotharan]], after the [[Starsplinters]]' conflict with the [[Badskab Buccaneers]] escalated in an unexpected way.{{Fn|1}}

