N'nkono Emba.wikitext:
{{SalamandersPortal}}
'''N'nkono Emba''' was a [[Pyre Guard|Pyre Guard Warden]] in the [[Salamanders]] [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]], who took part in the [[Horus Heresy]]'s [[Siege of Terra]].{{Fn|1a}}
==History==
He was among the [[Imperial]]s who were able to retreat within the [[Sanctum Imperialis]], as the [[Imperial Palace]] was overrun by [[Warmaster]] [[Horus]]' [[Traitor]] forces. Once inside, Emba was made one of [[Praetor (Rank)|Praetor]]-[[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Honfler]] officer line deputies{{Fn|1c}} of his twenty{{Fn|1b}} [[Denial Companies]] that were given to the Praetor-Captain to command by the [[War Court]].{{Fn|1c}} These were patchwork [[Space Marine Company|Companies]] of [[Legionaries]] who had also made it into the Sanctum Imperialis and the Denial commanders were sent to guard certain sections of the '''Delphic Wall'''. It served as a final defense against the Traitors trying to invade the Sanctum and Emba and his fellow deputies [[Aerim Lur]] and [[Tamos Roch]], aided Honfler in this task. However the Praetor-Captain's Companies did not take an active part in the defense. Following orders laid down by his [[Primarch]], [[Dorn]], Honfler instead held them in reserve until the section of the Wall his Companies defended was breached or scaled atop of by the Traitors.{{Fn|1b}}  

Once it became clear the '''Delphic Wall''' would fall to [[Horus]]' forces, though, the [[Denial Companies]] were withdrawn by the [[War Court]] into the [[Sanctum Imperialis]], to prepare for its invasion. They were then separated into groups of Companies, who would be commanded by [[Honfler]] or his deputies as they protected certain sections of the Sanctum. Emba would command five Companies and was sent to defend the Sanctum's '''Western Mass Passageway'''.{{Fn|1c}} By that point, though, [[Terra]] had become so infused by the [[Warp]],{{Fn|1d}} that the Traitor forces were able to materialize within the Sanctum Imperialis. The Denial Companies and other Imperials within the Sanctum were thus caught off guard, when they suddenly became attacked by the Traitors, even though its doors were still sealed.{{Fn|1e}} In the fighting that followed, the Denial Companies suffered heavy losses and Roch would be among those who lost their lives at the Traitors' hands.{{Fn|1f}}

