Naiall Fireheart.wikitext:
{{EldarPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' is the [[Eldar]] chieftain of [[Saim-Hann]]'s [[Clan Fireheart]].{{Fn|1a}}

An elderly and revered member of Saim-Hann who had once been a [[Spiritseer]], Naiall, by the time of the opening of the [[Great Rift]], he was ailing in health. However he still retained a sharp mind, and allowed his son [[Nuadhu Fireheart]] to take command of the many crisis' the clan faced due to the Great Rift. He was initially wary of Nuadhu's affiliation with the [[Ynnari]], but saw them as a possible counter to the machinations of rival clans on his own [[Craftworld]].{{Fn|1a}}

The source of Naiall's ailment was eventually revealed to be from his past as a Spiritseer. He had previously saved his wife [[Iyothia Icewhisper]] from being consumed by a [[Daemon]] but pulling her soul into his own body. Living with two souls was slowly killing him, but he refused to release her out of love and a sense of duty to protect her from torment at the hands of [[Slaanesh]]. At the climax of battle against the [[Necrons]] on [[Agarimethea]], Nuadhu and his daughter [[Caelledhin]] were able to convince Naiall to finally let Iyothia's soul go. The act returned him to vitality, and her death empowered [[Yvraine]] enough to turn the tide of the battle.{{Fn|1b}}

After the battle, Naiall fully accepted Nuadhu as a capable leader and let him become the new chieftain of Clan Fireheart.{{Fn|1c}}

