Naiao Servia.wikitext:
{{NurglePortal}}
'''Naiao Servia''' was the adjutant to the [[Planetary Governor]] of the [[Imperial]] world [[Forfoda]], who fell to [[Chaos]] and [[heresy]], worshipping the [[Chaos God]] [[Nurgle]].{{Fn|1}}


==Biography==
When the forces of the Imperium launched a campaign to retake Forfoda, Servia had holed up in the secondary spire complex of one of the planet's [[hive]]s. Although a squadron of [[Imperial Fists]] had marked the spire for destruction, [[Inquisitor Lord|Lord]] [[Joffen Tur]] of the [[Ordo Hereticus]] wished for Servia to be taken alive for questioning. To this end, he sent his [[interrogator]], [[Luce Spinoza]], to accompany the Fists' assault on the spire and ensure that his will be carried out.{{Fn|1}}

On reaching the spire's hub, the Imperials engaged Servia and her forces in battle. Servia fought a duel against [[Chaplain]] [[Erastus (Chaplain)|Erastus]] and managed to disarm him. Spinoza took up his fallen [[Crozius Arcanum|crozius]], [[Argent (Power Maul)|Argent]], and broke Servia's back before the mutant could kill the Chaplain. After Erastus and the rest of the Fists rallied, the Chaplain in turn ordered the Marines under his command to capture Servia alive and hand her over to Tur.{{Fn|1}}

The information that Tur and his agents extracted from Servia would later prove instrumental in retaking the industrial zones north of the spires, allowing the Imperium to turn the tide of the battle for Forfoda.{{Fn|1}}

