Nar Kezar.wikitext:
{{CSMPortal}}
{{Spoiler|source=Spear of the Emperor (Novel)}}
'''Nar Kezar''' is a [[Chaos Lord]] and '''Prince''' of the [[Pure (Chaos Warband)|Pure]] [[Warband]], which was once the [[Star Scorpions]] [[Chapter]] until they became lost in the [[Warp]]. 

==History==
Though the [[Imperium]] thought they had died, the Chapter was trapped in the Warp and remained there until the creation of the [[Great Rift]] freed them.  When they emerged back into their domain of [[Elara's Veil]], Kezar and the Star Scorpions had been fully corrupted by the forces of [[Chaos]].  They still thought themselves loyal to the Imperium though and returned to their [[Adeptus Astartes Homeworld|homeworld]], [[Khamun-Sen]], to regrow their numbers and resume their duties of protecting the worlds of the Veil.  However, their Brother Chapters of the [[Emperor's Spears]] and [[Celestial Lions]] discovered the [[Heresy]] that now marked the Scorpions and attacked them.  This ultimately led Kezar and his brethren to rename themselves the Pure and to begin a war of conquest against the Imperial worlds of the Veil.  Sometime later during their invasion, Kezar commanded the warship ''[[Venatrix Candidus]]'', when it began being pursued by the Spears' [[Strike Cruiser]], ''[[Hex]]''.  However, the ''Venatrix'' was able to ambush the ''Hex'' in turn and the Warband boarded it and took several prisoners before fleeing the stricken Strike Cruiser.  Among the prisoners was [[Lieutenant (Space Marine)|Lieutenant Commander]] [[Amadeus Kalus Incarius|Incarius]] of the [[Mentors]] Chapter, who Kezar took a personal interest in.{{Cite this}}

This was because the Mentors had been [[Founding|created]] to replace the Star Scorpions, after their disappearance and Kezar began interrogating Incarius for information about his Chapter.  The Commander refused to talk, however, despite the horrific tortures Kezar committed against him.  Though the Chaos Lord knew he would break Incarius down in time, the pursing ''Hex'' did not allow this to happen.  The Strike Cruiser had begun pursuing the ''Venatrix'' after the Pure's raid, and its crew had coordinated with other Imperial warships in the Veil to attack the Chaos warship.  While the ''Venatrix'' had been able to evade their attacks for a while, the Celestial Lions' Strike Cruiser, ''[[Blade of the Seventh Son]]'', finally ended the chase by ramming the warship.  This allowed the ''Son'' and ''Hex's'' [[Space Marine]]s to board the ''Venatrix''{{Fn|1a}} and free their captured comrades.  The Pure's forces aboard the ''Venatrix'' were all killed in the attack, save for Kezar himself, who was captured for interrogation aboard the ''Hex''.{{Fn|1b}}  

According to [[Anuradha Daaz]], Nar Kezar eventually escaped his captivity and unleashed great horrors upon the Emperor's Spears.{{Fn|1c}}

