Nasiem bal Tergu.wikitext:
{{SpaceMarinePortal}}
'''Nasiem Bal Tergu''' is the [[Primaris Captain]] of the [[Tome Keepers]] [[Chapter|Chapter's]] [[3rd Company (Tome Keepers)|Third Company]].{{Fn|1}}

==History==
[[Image:NasiemArt.jpg|thumb|right|220px|Nasiem bal Tergu{{Fn|3a}}]]
Born '''Nasiem''' of [[Istrouma]]'s '''House Tergu''', he later became the only [[Aspirant]] of his cycle to pass the [[Tome Keepers]] '''Trial of Pages'''.{{Fn|3b}} Nasiem would then go on to become a [[First Company]] [[Terminator Sergeant]], but at that time, the [[Chapter]] had suffered devastating losses both prior and after the creation of the [[Great Rift]]. The Tome Keepers had only a few hundred [[Battle Brothers]] left, when a [[Torchbearers]] fleet found them and gave the Chapter the gift of creating [[Primaris Space Marines]] and a large number of [[Greyshields]]. As the Tome Keepers began to rebuild themselves, Tergu was awarded the [[Space Marine Captain|Captaincy]] of the reforged [[3rd Company (Tome Keepers)|Third Company]], which was composed mainly of Primaris. In order to better understand his new charges{{Fn|1}}, Tergu was the first Tome Keeper to undergo the [[Rubicon Primaris]] and successfully emerged stronger than he was before.{{Fn|3b}} 

He later took part in the [[Argovon Campaign]], as part of the [[Indomitus Crusade]]'s [[Task Force XI]]. As the war against the [[Necron]] raged, Tergu served in the Task Force's senior command staff as a representative of the [[Space Marines]].{{Fn|2}}

==Wargear==
Tergu wields a [[power axe]] that is a heirloom of the [[Tome Keepers]] and was created thousands of years ago by his weaponsmith ancestors on the [[Chapter]]'s [[Adeptus Astartes Homeworld|Homeworld]]. Like all of the Tome Keeper's [[Battle Brothers]], the [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] also carries with him a tome that recounts his life work's.{{Fn|1}}

