Nekaybraianon.wikitext:
{{ChaosPortal}}
'''Nekaybraianon''' was a [[Daemon Prince]] who was pursued relentlessly by [[Inquisitor]] [[Adorjin]].{{Fn|1a}}

==History==
Adorjin was once a young and powerful [[psyker]] claimed by one of the [[Black Ships]] of the [[Inquisition]]. Through a series of terrible lapses in the Inquisition’s security, Nekaybraianon was able to possess the young Adorjin and slip unnoticed within her onto the Black Ship she had been claimed by. Using her body as his own he used her to commit terrible deeds upon her fellow passengers as they journeyed towards [[Terra]]. With the help of Inquisitor [[Mardaine]], who was eventually to become Adorjin's master, she managed the near impossible act of will of driving away Nekaybraianon.{{Fn|1a}} 

Mardaine took the young Adorjin as an [[acolyte]] and trained her in the ways of the [[Ordo Malleus]] until she was ready to hunt down the daemon that had violated her. Meanwhile Nekaybraianon had returned to real-space for some time, using the stolen flesh of psykers as it journeyed from world to world leaving a trail of [[Chaos Cult|cults]] it created on each one.  Adorjin spent her career tracking and destroying each lead, that lead her to her enemy. Finally the Daemon Prince was cornered by Adorjin when it tried to take refuge in another young psyker, hoping to slip past the Inquisitor by escaping on a Black Ship. The Inquisitor had planned for this and was there waiting for the daemon as the ship entered the warp.{{Fn|1a}}

Using the holy sword the ''[[Luminous Reproach]]'', gifted to her by the Inquisition, Adorjin fought Nekaybraianon, who had mutated the body of the psyker it possessed into a giant tentacled beast with gaping mouths lined with jagged fangs. After a long battle, Adorjin was finally able to drive the sword deep into the daemon's body, piercing its heart and giving it a [[True Death|permanent death]].{{Fn|1b}} Nekaybraianon’s psychic death throes killed not only the Inquisitor, but also the unwilling passengers and the crew of the vessel, leaving it adrift in the [[warp]].{{Fn|1a}}

